# Security OWASP Rule

Apply this rule to any code touching input handling, auth, storage, network, rendering, or dependencies.

## Mandatory Security Checks

- Validate and sanitize all external input server-side.
- Use parameterized queries; never build SQL/NoSQL queries with raw user input.
- Never hardcode secrets, tokens, or credentials.
- Avoid dangerous command execution with user-controlled arguments.
- Enforce authn/authz checks on protected endpoints and actions.
- Prevent IDOR and mass assignment with ownership checks and allowlisted fields.
- Keep sensitive tokens out of localStorage for auth flows.
- Return generic production errors; do not leak stacks or internals.

## Frontend Security

- Do not render unsanitized HTML (`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `v-html`, `innerHTML`).
- Avoid `eval` and dynamic code execution paths.
- Validate redirect targets to prevent open redirects.

## Operational Security

- Prefer strict headers (CSP, HSTS, nosniff, frame protections).
- Keep dependency risk visible (`pnpm audit` / lockfile hygiene).
- Log security events without logging sensitive values.

